# Elevation Law

**Principle:** Use a consistent shadow scale for depth. Z-index must follow a defined stacking order.

## Shadow Scale

| Level | Use Case | Example |
|-------|----------|---------|
| 0 | Flat | No shadow |
| 1 | Slight lift | Cards at rest |
| 2 | Hover, focus | Button hover |
| 3 | Raised | Dropdown, popover |
| 4 | Modal | Dialog, overlay |

**Example scale (8pt-aligned):**
```css
--shadow-soft: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
--shadow-medium: 0 8px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
--shadow-strong: 0 12px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
```

## Z-Index Scale

Define a stacking order — avoid arbitrary values.

| Layer | Z-Index | Use Case |
|-------|---------|----------|
| Base | 0 | Default |
| Sticky/fixed | 100 | Nav, header |
| Dropdown | 200 | Menus, popovers |
| Overlay | 300 | Backdrop |
| Modal | 400 | Dialogs |
| Toast | 500 | Notifications |
| Max | 9999 | Skip link, critical |

**Avoid:** Random z-index (e.g. 7, 23, 1047). Use the scale.

## Project Reference

This project: `STYLE-GUIDE.md` §1, §9. Use `var(--shadow-soft)`, `var(--shadow-medium)`, `var(--shadow-strong)`. Nav z-index: 100.
